{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Chemotactic, Anti-inflammatory", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Bridge", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Peptide discovery: predicted cathelicidin based on sequence alingment. Host expression: mainly expressed in spleen of the toad. Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence shows low similarity (38.1%) to PhD1 R: 20%, C: 17%. Activity: Active against A.hydrophila ATCC7966 (MIC >100 ug/ml), E.coli K12 (MIC > 100 ug/ml), L.monocytogenes ATCC19115 (MIC >100 ug/ml), P. mirabilis ATCC25933 (MIC 100 ug/ml), S.enterica ATCC13076 (MIC > 100 ug/ml), S. epidermidis ATCC12228 (MIC 12.5 ug/ml), S.iniae ATCC29178 (MIC > 100 ug/ml), V. harveyi ATCC33866 (MIC 25 ug/ml), V. parahaemolyticus ATCC33847 (MIC 100 ug/ml), and V. vulnifcus ATCC279562 (MIC 3.75 ug/ml). I Anti-inflammatory: Ll-CATH treatment decreased TNF-alpha and il-1beta expression in RAW264.7 cells (only at high concentration, to be confirmed).", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "39095814", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "BMC Vet Res. 2024 Aug 2;20(1):343. doi: 10.1186/s12917-024-04202-9. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP04778", "source_id": "AP04778", "source_numeric_id": "04778", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP04778", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Discovery of Ll-CATH: a novel cathelicidin from the Chong'an Moustache Toad (Leptobrachium liui) with antibacterial and immunomodulatory activity.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
